## Ticket Overview: tomd Paper Extraction Issues

### Missing or Empty Abstracts

Issues where the abstract is completely missing or the text fails to extract after the heading.

**P3692R4** [SOLVED]
Description: The entire abstract is missing.
Root cause: PDF paper. TOC body protection in `pipeline.py` counted only first-line words (`nxt_fl.split()`) instead of full paragraph words (`nxt_sec.text.split()`). P3692R4's abstract paragraph has 170 words total but only 8 on the first line, failing the `_TOC_BODY_PROTECT_MIN_WORDS=10` threshold. The abstract body was correctly extracted by MuPDF but then stripped as a TOC artifact.
Fix: Changed `nxt_fl.split()` to `nxt_sec.text.split()` in `pipeline.py`. Simulated across all 124 PDFs: only P3692R4 changes, 0 regressions.
File: `packages/tomd/src/tomd/lib/pdf/pipeline.py`

**P4043R0** [SOLVED]
Description: The abstract is empty. The "Abstract" heading is extracted, but the text that follows it is not.
Root cause: HTML paper. Abstract body was correctly extracted. The actual issue was a metadata leak: bold-formatted metadata lines (`**Document number**: P4043R0`, `**Date**: ...`, etc.) appeared in the Markdown body because `_REDUNDANT_META_RE` and `_FREEFORM_META_LABEL_RE` in `shared.py` did not match Markdown bold markers (`**...**`).
Fix: Extended both regexes with `\*{0,2}` anchors to match optional bold markers. Also added "Document number" as a label. Verified across 270 markdowns: 6 legitimate metadata leaks now stripped, zero false positives.
File: `packages/tomd/src/tomd/lib/shared.py`

**P4151R1** [SOLVED]
Description: The abstract is missing. It was present before; a recent code change led to this error.
Root cause: PDF paper. Abstract body is genuinely short (5 words). `total_words=5 < _TOC_BODY_PROTECT_MIN_WORDS=10`. The word-count threshold rejected the body as a TOC artifact.
Fix: Abstract-specific threshold bypass. When the protected heading is "abstract" (case-insensitive), the `_TOC_BODY_PROTECT_MIN_WORDS` check is skipped for the first body paragraph. Also affects P4151R0. Simulated across all 124 PDFs: only P4151R0 and P4151R1 change, 0 regressions.
File: `packages/tomd/src/tomd/lib/pdf/pipeline.py`

**P4042R0** [SOLVED]
Description: Abstract body missing.
Root cause: `_detect_body_size` in `structure.py` miscalculates body font size (9.0pt from LMRoman9-Regular wording text instead of 10.7pt Lato-Light prose). This causes the actual abstract body (10.7pt) to be classified as `HEADING` with `Confidence.LOW`, and the TOC protection loop breaks on `HEADING`.
Fix: In the TOC protection loop, when the protected heading is "abstract" and the first following section is a LOW-confidence HEADING, reclassify it as PARAGRAPH and protect it. Simulated across all 124 PDFs: only P4042R0 changes, 0 regressions.
File: `packages/tomd/src/tomd/lib/pdf/pipeline.py`

**P5000R0** [SOLVED]
Description: PDF body extraction is catastrophically incomplete. Only 1916 chars extracted. The PDF contains multiple sections (Revision History, Abstract, Tier 0: Safety, Profiles, etc.) but the markdown is missing most content.
Root cause: Phantom TOC detection. The plausibility guard lacked confirming signals (no dot leaders, no "Contents" label, no heading inside/outside overlap), causing legitimate body sections to be stripped as TOC artifacts.
Fix: TOC plausibility guard added to `pipeline.py`. Rejects phantom TOC detections without at least one confirming signal. Now extracts 5073 chars with all sections. Also fixed metadata heading duplication via `_strip_metadata_headings`.
File: `packages/tomd/src/tomd/lib/pdf/pipeline.py`

