### Extraction Boundary Issues / Over-Extraction

Issues where the abstract extracts correctly at first, but doesn't stop where it should, pulling in metadata, unrelated paragraphs, or swallowing other sections.

**P3977R0** [SOLVED]
Description: PDF paper. Title and metadata (Document, Date, Audience, Reply to) appeared as plaintext in the body.
Root cause: `_FREEFORM_META_LABEL_RE` in `shared.py` did not match bare "Document:" (only "Document number"/"Document No."). Additionally, continuation detection required indentation or comma prefix, but PDF metadata often has the value on the next line without indentation.
Fix: (1) Changed regex to make "number"/"No." optional after "Document" so bare "Document:" matches. (2) Extended continuation logic: when a metadata label line ends with ":" (value on next line), the next non-blank non-structural non-label line is treated as the value and also removed. (3) Plaintext title echo stripped by extending `strip_leading_h1` to match non-ATX titles via fuzzy `_titles_match`. (4) Bare "Abstract" promoted to `## Abstract` when it appears as the first content line after frontmatter. Simulated across 270 markdowns: 0 regressions.
File: `packages/tomd/src/tomd/lib/shared.py`

**P4030R0** [REMOVED]
No abstract in this paper. Not a bug.

**P4031R1** [SOLVED]
Works correctly after regeneration.

