### Missing Specific Elements / Sub-sections

Issues where the abstract is present, but specific related components are left out.

**P3625R1** [SOLVED]
Description: The abstract is present, but the following "Tony Table" is missing. The `[version.syn]` and `[concepts]` wording sections were also missing or had their content land in Acknowledgements.
Root cause: Four issues. (1) Tony Table cells are separate MuPDF blocks, not columnar lines within a block, so standard table detection missed them. (2) MuPDF delivered blocks out of y-order on page 1, causing version.syn and concepts wording content to land in Acknowledgements. (3) Wording section renderer collapsed all lines onto one line, destroying code structure. (4) Table cell code produced fragmented backticks.
Fix: (1) Added side-by-side table detection (`_detect_side_by_side_tables` in `table.py`) as Pass 2 after standard detection. (2) Added block sorting by `(page_num, y_midpoint)` in `pipeline.py` after `normalize_spans`. (3) `_render_wording_section` in `emit.py` now preserves line breaks when section contains monospace spans. (4) `_render_cell_spans` in `emit.py` merges all-monospace cell spans into single backtick pair.
Files: `table.py`, `pipeline.py`, `emit.py`

