### Table Cell Assembly Quality

Side-by-side table detection (Pass 2 in `table.py`) correctly identifies tables where each cell is a separate MuPDF block. Cell content assembly has remaining quality issues in some papers.

**Backtick fragmentation in code cells** [SOLVED]
Affected: All papers with monospace content in table cells (e.g. P3625R1 Tony Table).
Root cause: `_render_cell_spans` delegated to `_render_line_spans` which grouped consecutive monospace spans per Line object. Monospace grouping broke at block boundaries because non-monospace whitespace spans separated them.
Fix: `_render_cell_spans` in `emit.py` now detects when all non-whitespace spans are monospace and merges them into a single backtick pair.
File: `packages/tomd/src/tomd/lib/pdf/emit.py`

**Block ordering disrupts section boundaries** [SOLVED]
Affected: P3625R1 (version.syn/concepts content lands in Acknowledgements).
Root cause: MuPDF delivers blocks not in y-order within a page. No y-sort before structural analysis.
Fix: Both block lists sorted by `(page_num, y_midpoint)` in `pipeline.py` after `normalize_spans`, before table detection and structuring.
File: `packages/tomd/src/tomd/lib/pdf/pipeline.py`

**Multiline cell merging (missing spaces)** [OPEN]
Affected: p4099r0, p4100r0, p4172r0, p4096r0, p4089r0, p4090r0, p4094r0, p4095r0.
Root cause: Spans from multiple blocks are concatenated via `extend()` without inserting separator spans between blocks.

**Row overflow / column boundary breaks** [OPEN]
Affected: p4095r0, p3846r1, p4016r0.
Root cause: Raw pipe characters in cell text are not escaped before building the markdown table row.

Papers with side-by-side tables (24): Clean: p4088r0, p2583r3. Garbled cells: p4099r0, p4100r0, p4172r0, p4096r0, p4089r0, p4090r0, p4094r0, p4095r0, p4014r0, p4016r0, p3846r1, p4007r0, p4003r1, p3932r0, p4098r0, p4182r0. Not detected: p2034r6, p3427r3, p3970r0. Pre-existing empty: p3839r0.

