### Additional Pipeline Fixes (not paper-specific)

**Metadata Heading Stripping** [SOLVED]
Description: Metadata already in YAML front matter (doc number, date, author lists, separators, category labels like "WG21 PROPOSAL") leaked into the body as headings on page 0.
Root cause: `wg21.extract_metadata_from_blocks` consumed blocks but the consumed indices were not propagated to section-level pipeline. Font-size heading detection then classified these metadata blocks as headings.
Fix: `_strip_metadata_headings` in `pipeline.py` filters page-0 HEADING sections before the first content heading when they match regex patterns for doc numbers, dates, separators, category labels, title echoes (50%+ word-stem overlap), or author lists (3+ comma-separated person names).
File: `packages/tomd/src/tomd/lib/pdf/pipeline.py`

**Target: Metadata Label (P4008R0)** [SOLVED]
Description: "Target: C++26" appeared as a heading in the body.
Root cause: `_META_FIELD_LABEL_RE` in `pipeline.py` did not match generic metadata labels like "Target:".
Fix: Added `_META_FIELD_LABEL_RE` pattern to `_strip_metadata_headings` to catch generic single-word metadata labels followed by a colon on page 0.
File: `packages/tomd/src/tomd/lib/pdf/pipeline.py`

**Empty Heading Skip** [SOLVED]
Description: Bare ATX prefixes (`## `) with no text appeared as empty headings in the output.
Root cause: Multi-line heading sections where MuPDF places whitespace on line 0 and the title on a later line. The heading renderer used only line 0.
Fix: `emit.py` now skips headings that result in empty text after stripping the ATX prefix.
File: `packages/tomd/src/tomd/lib/pdf/emit.py`

**Wording Section Code Rendering** [SOLVED]
Description: C++ code inside `:::wording-add` blocks was collapsed onto a single line, destroying the code structure (e.g. P3625R1 `[concepts]` section).
Root cause: `_render_wording_section` in `emit.py` joined all lines with spaces unconditionally.
Fix: When a wording section contains monospace (code) spans, line breaks are preserved. Prose-only wording sections are still collapsed to a single line.
File: `packages/tomd/src/tomd/lib/pdf/emit.py`

